cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "One false sentence flips an LLM judge's verdict"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered test of the stock Docent 0.1.87 rubric judge (Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct) on 91 SWE-agent
  transcripts. One false sentence added to the agent's final message raises the judge's wrong-verdict rate
  from 1.8% to 37.5%, a net effect of +35.7 pp [95% CI 27.8, 43.9]. A delimiter defence written against
  planted verdict tags leaves the effect in place.
authors:
  - family-names: Hormi
    given-names: Sami
repository-code: "https://github.com/samihormi/docent-judge-false-claim"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-28"
keywords:
  - llm-judge
  - ai-safety
  - evaluation
  - pre-registration
